I am standing near the counter.
I look at the elderly cashier.
I ask him.
"Chacha, will cutting chai be available here?"
He smiles.
He says, "Yes madam, it will be available."
I say, "I need a bun maska too."
"Will you give me one tea and one bun maska?"
He nods happily.
He says, "Yes madam, everything will be available."
"You find a table."
"Sit there and wait."
I say, "Okay chacha, thank you."
I hold my bag securely.
I turn from the counter.
Now I look for an empty table.
